==============================================================================
Provenance of benchmark task templates
==============================================================================

The benchmark task templates under `task/` fall into two groups with different
provenance:

1. Tasks 01-59 (Static Routing, RIP, OSPF, BGP)

   The network scenarios underlying these templates are derived from the
   publicly archived GNS3Vault lab collection, now maintained by
   NetworkLessons:

       https://github.com/networklessons/labs/tree/main/gns3vault-archive

   From each lab we reused the *technical substance* — the topology structure,
   the protocol feature under exercise, and the configuration objective. We did
   NOT redistribute any file from that collection: no `.gns3` project files, no
   topology images, and no startup/solution configuration files from the
   original labs are included here.

   Every template in this repository was re-authored for NetConfArena:
   device names, interface assignments and IP addressing are generated by our
   parameterization layer (`task/task_loader.py` plus per-task `params.yaml`),
   the reference configurations were re-written and re-verified against the
   emulator, and all executable test cases are original to this work.

   The original labs carry no open-source license. Their public availability
   does not by itself grant permission to copy, adapt, distribute, or relicense
   their contents. Attribution is provided here; anyone wishing to reuse the
   original lab material itself should consult NetworkLessons.

2. Tasks 60-96 (MPLS LDP / TE / L3VPN, L2VPN, IP overlay)

   Authored by the NetConfArena authors. No third-party lab material is
   involved.


==============================================================================
Third-party software and images not distributed here
==============================================================================

Running NetConfArena requires software that this repository does NOT include
and does NOT license:

  * GNS3 server (https://gns3.com) — installed separately by the user.
  * Cisco IOS images for the Dynamips platforms used by the task templates
    (e.g. c7200-adventerprisek9-mz.124-24.T5, c3640-a3js-mz.124-25d).
    These are proprietary Cisco software. Users must obtain them through
    their own valid Cisco license; they are not redistributed by this project.

See README.md ("Environment setup") for details.
